<reference id="ReinitializeDeviceWindow-BACnetGuid-3A37B299" xml:lang="en" class="- topic/topic       reference/reference "><title class="- topic/title ">ReinitializeDevice window</title><shortdesc class="- topic/shortdesc ">This window configures a password, which the driver requires
when someone reboots a Supervisor station or needs to apply pending changes without a complete restart.</shortdesc><prolog class="- topic/prolog "><metadata class="- topic/metadata "><keywords class="- topic/keywords "><indexterm class="- topic/indexterm ">ReinitializeDevice window</indexterm></keywords></metadata></prolog><refbody class="- topic/body        reference/refbody "><section class="- topic/section "><fig class="- topic/fig "><title class="- topic/title ">Reinitialize Device properties</title><image placement="break" scale="65" scope="local" href="../graphic/windowReinitializeDevice_0000080512.png" class="- topic/image "/></fig><p class="- topic/p ">To open this window, in the Supervisor station, expand <menucascade class="+ topic/ph ui-d/menucascade "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Config</uicontrol><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Drivers</uicontrol></menucascade>, double-click <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">BacnetAwsNetwork</uicontrol> and click <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Reinit</uicontrol>.</p></section><properties class="- topic/simpletable reference/properties "><prophead class="- topic/sthead      reference/prophead "><proptypehd class="- topic/stentry     reference/proptypehd ">Property</proptypehd><propvaluehd class="- topic/stentry     reference/propvaluehd ">Value</propvaluehd><propdeschd class="- topic/stentry     reference/propdeschd ">Description</propdeschd></prophead><property class="- topic/strow       reference/property "><proptype class="- topic/stentry     reference/proptype ">Reinitialize Command</proptype><propvalue class="- topic/stentry     reference/propvalue ">drop-down list (defaults to <option class="+ topic/keyword pr-d/option ">Warm Start</option>)</propvalue><propdesc class="- topic/stentry     reference/propdesc ">Selects the type of reboot or reinitialization that requires the password.<p class="- topic/p "><option class="+ topic/keyword pr-d/option ">Warm Start</option> requires a password when someone clicks
the Windows menu followed by <menucascade class="+ topic/ph ui-d/menucascade "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Power</uicontrol><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Restart</uicontrol></menucascade>. It may also be used to apply pending changes to a Network Port object(s) in the remote device.</p><p class="- topic/p "><option class="+ topic/keyword pr-d/option ">Cold Start</option> requires a password when someone clicks the Windows menu followed
by <menucascade class="+ topic/ph ui-d/menucascade "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Power</uicontrol><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Shutdown</uicontrol></menucascade>.</p><p class="- topic/p "><option class="+ topic/keyword pr-d/option ">Activate Changes</option> requires a password when someone needs to apply pending changes to a Network Port object(s) in the remote device (as of <keyword conkeyref="wh_variables_n4/niagara4.15" class="- topic/keyword "/>).</p></propdesc></property><property class="- topic/strow       reference/property "><proptype class="- topic/stentry     reference/proptype ">Password</proptype><propvalue class="- topic/stentry     reference/propvalue ">text</propvalue><propdesc class="- topic/stentry     reference/propdesc ">Defines the password.</propdesc></property></properties></refbody></reference>